.Dd 2026-06-02
.Dt NOMAD-CHECK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-check
.Nd pre-flight and health inventory of the host, stack, and install
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad check
.Op Cm system | stack | install | all
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
inspects the machine and the NOMAD deployment and prints a findings report.
Run it before an install to confirm the host is ready, or after one to confirm
the stack is healthy.
.Pp
The optional argument selects which section to run.
With no argument,
.Nm
runs every section.
.Pp
Output is written to the terminal and also tee'd, with ANSI color stripped, to
.Pa nomad-check-<timestamp>.log
and
.Pa nomad-check-latest.log
in the directory the
.Nm nomad
script lives in, so a run can be reviewed or synced later.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm system
Check the host: hardware, OS, RAM, and related prerequisites.
.It Cm stack
Check the running NOMAD stack and its services.
For each Ollama instance this runs a real inference probe
.Pq a one-token generate for chat, an embed for the embed-only daemon
so a missing llama.cpp runner is caught, not just a responsive
.Pq Li /api/tags
port.
.It Cm install
Inventory the installation, including whether the llama.cpp runner
.Pq Li llama-server
is present.
.Cm inventory
is an accepted alias.
.It Cm all
Run system, stack, and install in sequence.
This is the default.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad check
Run the full inventory across all sections.
.It Ic nomad check system
Check only the host prerequisites.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-system 1
